{"title":"2016 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Complementary_Counting)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Complementary Counting)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3(One_Sentence!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3(One Sentence!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two different numbers are randomly selected from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/5/b151b79dfb9671886fffc3dd3a6383c1f88fb41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{ - 2, -1, 0, 3, 4, 5\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"143\" height=\"20\" /> and multiplied together. What is the probability that the product is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/4/a54165a617e820bab785a62aa15b21c3e1fa5213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\dfrac{1}{6}\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }\\dfrac{1}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }\\dfrac{1}{4}\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }\\dfrac{1}{3}\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\dfrac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"375\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>1. Identify the total number of ways to select two different numbers from the set:\n</p><p>The set has 6 elements. The number of ways to choose 2 different numbers from 6 is given by the combination formula: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffa257c97c0eceb611fae76d9c3616c0c06848d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{6}{2} = \\frac{6 \\times 5}{2 \\times 1} = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"150\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p><p>2. Identify the favorable outcomes:\n</p><p>For the product to be zero, one of the chosen numbers must be zero. The set contains one zero (0). To have a product of zero, we need to choose 0 and any other number from the remaining five numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/3/8836f7150a38b281c401fb058005e5df705e5c37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2, -1, 3, 4, 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>The number of ways to choose 0 and one other number from the remaining five is 5.\n</p><p>3. Calculate the probability:\n</p><p>The probability is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of outcomes: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d12659500c33c9c7e421e69b5d79333dd4b18d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{Probability} = \\frac{\\text{Number of favorable outcomes}}{\\text{Total number of outcomes}} = \\frac{5}{15} = \\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"417\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the probability that the product is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/3/ef3916b929b4908717522eb1dbd423a62cf66118.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} \\ \\frac{1}{3}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"66\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~GeometryMystery\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Complementary_Counting.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Complementary_Counting)\">Solution 2 (Complementary Counting)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Complementary Counting)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Because the only way the product of the two numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is if one of the numbers we choose is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/d/ced6b9b2e75857b566f1e516560c4a4d63977299.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> we calculate the probability of NOT choosing a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/4/604c735470dd0152ca1cff75fe26eadf5cef7f49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/d/f1d6190fa6e314c6c40359ade07134755ad8525e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{6} \\cdot \\frac{4}{5} = \\frac{2}{3}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"80\" height=\"37\" /> Therefore our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b982b2477bee17d72ecf9f4e08a5ecd6e79fe24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 - \\frac{2}{3} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} \\ \\frac{1}{3}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"131\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_3.28One_Sentence.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3(One_Sentence!!!)\">Solution 3(One Sentence!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3(One Sentence!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>1/6 * Any other number + Any other number * 1/6 = 1/6+1/6 = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/6/546d31a1471ef0f810d1a61732eb1c11fb062741.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} \\ \\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"61\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>-JasonDaGoat\n</p><p><br />\n1/6 Chance of 0 * A number in the set + 1/6 chance of A number in the set * 0 = 1/6+1/6 = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/6/546d31a1471ef0f810d1a61732eb1c11fb062741.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} \\ \\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"61\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>- edited by TTDBJ\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>To get a product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, one of the numbers must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which means that we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/5/3756515091c11bf36cf17d909f9623e9583c5262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2P1=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"14\" /> possible combinations of a random number from the set, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. There is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> total possible products, giving us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/8363ecc686113b1d0cce7b74ec234541e43302f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"24\" height=\"48\" />.\n-Electric_Cheetah_88\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING!!!)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/cRsvq0BH4MI\">https://youtu.be/cRsvq0BH4MI</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/6xNkyDgIhEE?t=357\">https://youtu.be/6xNkyDgIhEE?t=357</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/jDeS4A6N-nE\">https://youtu.be/jDeS4A6N-nE</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8\" title=\"2016 AMC 8\">2016 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2016 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2016\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2016 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2016 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 AMC 8 Problems